---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import CTASection from '../../components/CTASection.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How Much Does Pressure Washing Cost in Kissimmee? (2026)"
  description="Honest pressure washing cost ranges for Kissimmee & Central Florida homes. Driveways, houses, pool decks. What drives price and how to get accurate estimates."
  ogImage="/images/power-washing.jpg"
  schema={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@graph": [
      {
        "@type": "Article",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pressure-washing-cost-kissimmee/#article",
        "headline": "How Much Does Pressure Washing Cost in Kissimmee? (2026)",
        "description": "Honest cost ranges for pressure washing in Kissimmee. What drives price and how to estimate.",
        "author": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC."
        },
        "publisher": {
          "@type": "Organization",
          "name": "GO PRO HOME IMPROVEMENTS INC.",
          "logo": {
            "@type": "ImageObject",
            "url": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/images/logo.png"
          }
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
        "@id": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pressure-washing-cost-kissimmee/#breadcrumbs",
        "itemListElement": [
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 1,
            "name": "Home",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 2,
            "name": "Guides",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides"
          },
          {
            "@type": "ListItem",
            "position": 3,
            "name": "Pressure Washing Cost",
            "item": "https://goprohomeimprovements.com/guides/pressure-washing-cost-kissimmee"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }}
>
  <Header />

  <section class="bg-gopro-charcoal text-white py-16 border-b-4 border-gopro-orange">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <nav class="text-sm mb-6 font-sans">
        <a href="/" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <a href="/guides" class="text-gray-400 hover:text-gopro-orange transition-colors">Guides</a>
        <span class="mx-2 text-gray-500">/</span>
        <span class="text-white">Pressure Washing Cost</span>
      </nav>
      <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-4 tracking-tight">How Much Does Pressure Washing Cost in Kissimmee? (2026)</h1>
      <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 max-w-3xl font-sans">
        Honest cost ranges for driveways, houses, pool decks, and patios. What drives price in Central Florida.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding">
    <div class="container-custom">
      <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <p class="text-xl text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-6 font-sans">
            <a href="/services/power-washing" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Pressure washing</a> costs in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, and Central Florida depend on square footage, surface type, and how dirty it is. Here are real ranges from 15+ years washing Florida homes, driveways, and pool decks.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Pressure Washing Cost by Surface</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Driveways</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Single-car driveway (200-300 sq ft):</strong> $100-$175</li>
            <li><strong>Two-car driveway (400-600 sq ft):</strong> $175-$275</li>
            <li><strong>Large driveway (700-1,000 sq ft):</strong> $250-$400</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Concrete driveways with heavy black mildew stains or oil spots take longer and cost more. Fresh dirt washes fast. Most <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a> driveways fall in the $150-$250 range.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">House Exteriors</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small house (1,000-1,500 sq ft):</strong> $200-$350</li>
            <li><strong>Medium house (1,500-2,500 sq ft):</strong> $300-$500</li>
            <li><strong>Large house (2,500-3,500 sq ft):</strong> $450-$700</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Price depends on siding type (vinyl, stucco, Hardie board), number of stories, and mildew coverage. North-facing walls with heavy green algae take more time and chemicals. If you're washing before <a href="/services/interior-exterior-painting" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">painting</a>, budget for the high end.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Pool Decks & Patios</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Small patio/deck (150-250 sq ft):</strong> $75-$150</li>
            <li><strong>Medium pool deck (300-500 sq ft):</strong> $150-$275</li>
            <li><strong>Large pool deck + patio (600-1,000 sq ft):</strong> $250-$450</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Pool decks in Central Florida collect green algae fast from splashed water and humidity. Pavers cost slightly more than flat concrete because of grout lines. Travertine and natural stone need lower pressure (soft wash) to avoid damage.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">Fences & Decks</h3>
          <ul class="list-none space-y-2 mb-6 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>Wood fence (per linear foot):</strong> $1-$3</li>
            <li><strong>Vinyl fence (per linear foot):</strong> $0.75-$2</li>
            <li><strong>Wood deck (200-400 sq ft):</strong> $150-$350</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Wood fences and decks need lower pressure than concrete to avoid splintering. If you're staining or sealing after washing, add drying time (2-3 days in Florida humidity).
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What Drives Pressure Washing Cost?</h2>
          
          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">1. Square Footage</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            More area = more time = higher cost. Most contractors charge by the job (not hourly), but square footage is the biggest factor in their quote.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">2. Surface Type</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Concrete handles high pressure. Vinyl siding, wood, and painted surfaces need soft wash (low pressure + cleaning solution). Soft wash takes longer and costs 10-20% more than straight pressure washing.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">3. How Dirty It Is</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Light dust washes fast. Heavy mildew, black algae, or oil stains require pre-treatment, stronger chemicals, and multiple passes. If your driveway or house hasn't been washed in 3+ years, expect quotes at the higher end.
          </p>

          <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide mt-8">4. Accessibility</h3>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Second-story siding, hard-to-reach soffits, or properties with dense landscaping take longer. Easy access = lower cost.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gopro-orange/10 border-l-4 border-gopro-orange p-6 my-8">
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-0">
              <strong>Florida factor:</strong> Central Florida's year-round humidity and sun cause algae and mildew to grow faster than cooler climates. Most homes need pressure washing every 12-18 months to stay ahead of the green. Letting it go 3+ years means heavier buildup and higher cleaning costs.
            </p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">Bundling Saves Money</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Washing multiple surfaces in one visit costs less than separate trips. Common bundles:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li><strong>House + driveway:</strong> $350-$650</li>
            <li><strong>Driveway + pool deck + patio:</strong> $300-$550</li>
            <li><strong>Full exterior package</strong> (house, driveway, pool deck, walkways): $600-$1,000</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We're already on-site with equipment set up, so adding extra surfaces costs less per square foot than if you called us back separately.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">What's Included in the Cost?</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            A complete pressure washing quote should include:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Pre-treatment (mildew remover, degreaser if needed)</li>
            <li>Pressure washing or soft wash</li>
            <li>Rinsing and spot treatment</li>
            <li>Basic debris cleanup (we don't haul plants or furniture, but we rinse debris off surfaces)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            If a quote seems too cheap, ask what's included. Some contractors skip pre-treatment or rush the job, which leaves streaks and doesn't fully remove mildew.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">How to Get an Accurate Estimate</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            No one can give you an exact price over the phone without seeing the property. We need to:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Measure the area (driveway, house exterior, pool deck)</li>
            <li>Check surface condition (light dirt vs. heavy mildew)</li>
            <li>Identify surface type (concrete, stucco, vinyl, pavers)</li>
            <li>Note access issues (two-story, tight spaces)</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            We do free estimates in <a href="/areas/kissimmee" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Kissimmee</a>, <a href="/areas/orlando" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Orlando</a>, <a href="/areas/celebration" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">Celebration</a>, and Central Florida. Takes 10-15 minutes on-site, and you get a written quote with all costs itemized.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">DIY vs. Hiring a Pro</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Renting a pressure washer costs $50-$100/day. Add cleaning chemicals ($20-$40), and you're at $70-$140 to do it yourself. Sounds cheaper than hiring a pro, but:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 mb-6 space-y-2 text-gray-700 font-sans">
            <li>Wrong pressure settings damage siding, strip paint, gouge wood, or crack vinyl</li>
            <li>DIY takes 3-5 hours for a driveway that a pro finishes in 45 minutes</li>
            <li>You're responsible for equipment problems or injuries</li>
          </ul>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            For small patios or single driveways, DIY might make sense. For house exteriors or large areas, the time and risk aren't worth the $100-$200 savings.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl font-display font-black uppercase mb-6 tracking-tight mt-12">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-lg text-gray-700 mb-6 font-sans">
            Pressure washing in Kissimmee costs $100-$300 for driveways, $200-$600 for house exteriors, $75-$450 for pool decks and patios. What drives price: square footage, surface type, how dirty it is, and accessibility. Bundling multiple surfaces saves 10-20%. Get an on-site estimate for accurate pricing—free in Central Florida.
          </p>

          <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-lg p-8 my-8">
            <h3 class="text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase mb-4 tracking-wide">Need Pressure Washing in Kissimmee?</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 font-sans mb-6">
              We wash driveways, house exteriors, pool decks, patios, and more. Free estimates, fair pricing, and we use the right pressure for each surface.
            </p>
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4">
              <a href="/estimate" class="btn-primary">
                Get Free Estimate
              </a>
              <a href="tel:4072446873" class="btn-secondary">
                Call (407) 244-6873
              </a>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200">
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 font-sans">
              <a href="/guides" class="text-gopro-orange hover:underline">← Back to All Guides</a>
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTASection
    title="Professional Pressure Washing"
    description="Driveways, houses, pool decks. Fair pricing, quality work. Serving Central Florida."
  />

  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
